    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_05cc279c9641dc64eada69fbb400ec3ff0490ac816950d1829b2a1e52e026dae",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source-grounded mathematics: choosing the exponential parameter at scale √A/log A and using polynomial powers bounded by exponentials converts the previous estimate into L^p tail decay of order log(2+A)/√(1+A) on off-real compacts. Small A is handled separately by Minkowski and exponential moments of a bounded-window count. Hence ξ_∞'/ξ_∞ belongs to every finite L^p off R, and products of its values are limits of moments of bounded spatial truncations. Conceptual interpretation: uniform integrability is the missing bridge from a conditionally regularized random resolvent to legitimate expectation calculations; finite windows expose sine-kernel correlations, while L^p decay licenses removal of the window.",
