    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3aec6c2060eef89a3a4997972a647504049adac7a2d1864127ff8c75ed84633f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Centered sine-process statistics extend continuously to H^{1/2}. For a dilated smooth test, the variance error and every cumulant of order at least three are bounded by Fourier-tail integrals whose thresholds move outward with the dilation, so those bounds vanish while the |k|-weighted quadratic covariance remains; density then extends the Gaussian finite-dimensional limit to all H^{1/2} tests. Applying this to the off-real Stieltjes family f_z(t)=1/(z-t) identifies the statistic with the centered logarithmic derivative, and uniform increment bounds plus a vanishing-contour argument turn the finite-dimensional blue-noise limit into compact-open convergence to a holomorphic Gaussian field.",
