    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5d87c8b1a2b177179720059391cd9a5687d07dc29a75efcdb98afca3c5119e27",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After mean-spacing normalization, both logarithmic derivatives have the same regularized zero-resolvent form: ξ_∞'/ξ_∞ is iπ plus a paired sine-point sum, while the finite-height Hadamard calculation for zeta gives iπ plus a paired sum over locally rescaled zeta zeros and an o(1) error. Rigidity makes index-symmetric and spatially symmetric cutoffs equivalent. Subtracting the Lebesgue background then identifies the sine resolvent with the Stieltjes linear statistic X_{f_z}; blue-noise dilation gives its finite-dimensional Gaussian limit, and covariance, contour, and tightness arguments upgrade that limit to a holomorphic Gaussian field off the real axis.",
